{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"prior finding 0","checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the broad '(failure)' marker cannot swallow a genuine lease move that lacks a 'stale info' token, and document the assumption.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:735: _NON_CAS_REJECT_MARKERS += (\"fatal error in commit_refs\", \"(failure)\")  # bug ebee: GH 5xx","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:744-748: 'stale info' returns True before the non-CAS markers are consulted, so the posture stays fail-closed but hinges on 'stale info' always appearing for a real move"],"finding":"The '(failure)' marker added to _NON_CAS_REJECT_MARKERS is very broad: GitHub prints '(failure)' on essentially any '! [remote rejected] ... (failure)' line. Because _is_cas_mismatch_stderr checks 'stale info' first it stays safe for lease pushes, but any future ambiguous rejection carrying '(failure)' will now silently fail-closed as non-CAS; the token relies on 'stale info' always co-occurring for a genuine lease move.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py:735","norm_id":"n0c20add23cbf46ed","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes",